langen^"He continued this diligently while on the field of battle,^@^ and immediately showing his appreciation for his troops' military exploits motivated them in an extremely significant fashion.^@^  Also, whenever one of his troops was brought down by an illness, he would be the first to rush up to them and care for them, and so on.^@^  ...Takeda Shingen wasn't just the man who led the strongest calvary corps in the warring period.^@^  He was the person who cared the most for his troops throughout the warring period."^\
